# What never reaches the Docker build context.
#
# The build copies `requirements.txt` and `apps/api` and nothing else, but the
# *context* is the repo root — so without this file the daemon receives the whole
# working tree first, including a multi-gigabyte `.venv` and `node_modules`. That
# is the difference between a build that starts in a second and one that spends a
# minute uploading files it will discard.
#
# It is also a **secrets boundary**, and that is the half worth stating: `.env`
# holds the deployment's JWT secret, database password, and LLM API key. It is
# gitignored, so nothing stops it being copied into an image otherwise — and an
# image is pushed to a registry where a `.env` layer is readable by anyone who
# can pull it.

# --- Secrets ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Virtual environments and caches ---
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- Frontend: not part of the API image ---
apps/web/
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# --- Version control and CI ---
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.dockerignore

# --- Tests and documentation: not shipped in the runtime image ---
tests/
docs/
context/
README.md
LICENSE
CLAUDE.md

# --- Editor and OS noise ---
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
